      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given a set of three numbers with a mean and median both equal to 4, and the smallest number is 1, we need to find the range of the set.\n\nLet's denote the three numbers in ascending order as \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) where \\(a = 1\\). The mean of the three numbers is given by:\n\\[\n\\frac{a + b + c}{3} = 4\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(a = 1\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{1 + b + c}{3} = 4\n\\]\nMultiplying both sides by 3, we obtain:\n\\[\n1 + b + c = 12\n\\]\nSubtracting 1 from both sides, we get:\n\\[\nb + c = 11\n\\]\nSince the median of the set is also 4, the middle number \\(b\\) must be 4. Thus, we have:\n\\[\nb = 4\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(b = 4\\) into the equation \\(b + c = 11\\), we get:\n\\[\n4 + c = 11\n\\]\nSubtracting 4 from both sides, we obtain:\n\\[\nc = 7\n\\]\nSo, the set of numbers is \\(1, 4, 7\\). The range of the set is the difference between the largest and smallest numbers:\n\\[\n\\text{Range} = 7 - 1 = 6\n\\]\nTherefore, the range of the set of numbers is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
